## Interface: 16001, 120105
## Title: Combat
## Notes: Sane UI's frames for the fight, being built. Your frame, your target's and your focus's in a nameplate's look, their targets and your pet under them, your cast and breath part of your frame; rings around the mouse for your global cooldown and cast; one frame for your party and raid, up to forty, sized in Edit Mode; a threat and damage meter of your group; the game's action bars clean, only the buttons that hold something; frames and bars out of sight at rest. Docked at the screen's bottom middle: push the mouse against the middle of the bottom edge, or press your spellbook or talents key, and our own talents and spellbook fill the screen side by side, as the game's; push there again, or Esc, and they go back.
## Author: Saneroki
## Version: 0.3.0
## Category: Sane UI
## Group: SaneUI
## Dependencies: SaneUI
## IconTexture: Interface\Icons\Ability_DualWield
## X-License: MIT

# The module's own table, its words and settings. First: the other files will add to that table.
Combat.lua
# Its window: docked at the bottom middle, filling the screen from the middle half of the bottom edge
Window.lua
# The full screen's windows on Core's board: each registers itself (Board.Part); the talent planner seated
Board.lua
# Talents: our own window of your talents, as the game's (Talents/)
# The part on the board: the game's shared talent frame loaded, fitted into its panel, its words
Talents\Talents.lua
# The nodes: the game's shared node buttons with the class talents' glow, tooltip and sounds; the arrows
Talents\Nodes.lua
# What the trees stand on: the class's picture, its clouds and lights, the frame and dividers, the commit's flash
Talents\Art.lua
# Each tree's head with the points spent in it, and the unspent points
Talents\Headers.lua
# The primary and secondary specialization: the game's tabs, Active or Activate
Talents\Specs.lua
# Apply Changes, Undo and the Reset menu at the foot
Talents\Foot.lua
# The commit's and the switch's cast over the trees, on a cast bar of ours from the game's template
Talents\Commit.lua
# Buying, refunding, applying, undoing and resetting, where the game allows it
Talents\Changes.lua
# The frame: the game's shared talent frame with the class layer over it, its events while shown
Talents\Tree.lua
# Spellbook: our own window of your spells, as the game's (Book/)
# Where each entry stands on the pages, by the game's rules (lists in, lists out)
Book\Layout.lua
# What the book holds: the game's tabs, their spells as its book shows them, the search
Book\Data.lua
# One entry, as the game's: its icon and frame, name, rank, cooldown, the glow of a spell on no bar
Book\Item.lua
# The game's secure buttons over the icons, which cast out of a fight
Book\Casts.lua
# The book itself: its pages, tabs, the game's paging controls and settings
Book\Book.lua
# Your spellbook, pet book and talents keys opening ours (the game's override bindings; our keys: Bindings.xml)
Keys.lua
# A mark beside a creature's nameplate while it belongs to an objective of your quests still to do
QuestMarks.lua
# Rings around the mouse for the global cooldown and your cast, only while they run
MouseRings.lua
# Unit frames: ours for you, your target and your focus, in a nameplate's look, in place of the game's (Units/)
# The bar: round and green, its border, the rank's line, the glow, the power line; the row under it
Units\Bar.lua
# The line inside it: level and raid marker left, then the name, the health right; the row's name
Units\Text.lua
# The auras that matter most around them, in the game's own aura containers; the right click on an icon
Units\Auras.lua
# Your lists Always show and Never show, and their window (/sane auras)
Units\Lists.lua
# Your cast as part of your frame, in place of the game's cast bar
Units\Cast.lua
# Your breath and the game's other timers on you as part of your frame, in place of its bars
Units\Timers.lua
# The frames and their rows (their targets, your pet): the game's secure unit buttons, placed in Edit Mode
Units\Units.lua
# Your party and raid: which of your buffs a member is missing, one member's frame, the tools behind your own slot, and
# the one window for them all
Units\GroupBuffs.lua
Units\GroupFace.lua
Units\GroupTools.lua
Units\Group.lua
# Reminders of buffs and debuffs: what shows when, the invisible bars, the right click on the game's auras, the window
Reminders\Reminders.lua
Reminders\Bars.lua
Reminders\Clicks.lua
Reminders\Editor.lua
# The game's action bars clean: only the buttons that hold something, each its icon alone
ActionBars.lua
# The game's experience and stance bars out of sight, its menu bar on mouseover
GameBars.lua
# The threat and damage meter: threat added up, what the game tells of a fight, the fights and saved ones, one character's
# row, the buttons on the first line, the window
Meter\Threat.lua
Meter\Read.lua
Meter\Fights.lua
Meter\Row.lua
Meter\Controls.lua
